On 05-May-98 Jeff DeMaagd wrote:
> 
> Has anyone gotten DOSemu working under Alpha?  I suspect that it wouldn't
> work as of yet directly, but would running DOSemu under em86 work?  Is
> there an em86 FAQ on azstarnet?
> 
> There are a few DOS programs that I want to use yet, and I want to use
> them in any environment possible, which hopefully includes Alpha Linux.

DOSEMU does not and will never work on the Alpha. It depends on having a *real*
i86 processor available since it does not emulated the x86 chip itself.

Your options are PCEMU or Bochs. Bochs works well enough to run Windows '95 but
it is slow, even on a 533Mhz. machine.


