Jeff DeMaagd wrote:

> > Your options are PCEMU or Bochs. Bochs works well enough to run Windows '95 but
> > it is slow, even on a 533Mhz. machine.
> 
> Where do I find either program and their "official" pages?

Bochs can be found at http://www.world.com/~bochs

pcemu can be found at:

ftp.cs.bris.ac.uk/users/hedley/

Be aware that pcemu only emulates the 8086 CPU so if you need anything
fancier you will need to check out Bochs.

There are also some commercial emulators from Insignia Solutions but I
don't think they support Linux and the products are costly. SunPC is one
example, but it is for SunOS/Solaris.

