Before I say how I figured out a solution the problem I posted a
couple of days ago, I had one more question: how does one set a MILO
variable in the AlphaBIOS? Does one just do:

boot sda3:boot/vmlinuz.gz root=/dev/sda3 MEMORY_SIZE=256?

for the options line?

Normally, I'd type in "set MEMORY_SIZE 256" at the MILO> prompt, but
of course, I'd like to automate this process.  Right now, it
recognises only 0 megabytes which causes all sorts of problems.  There
is an erratum about it in the RedHat page, about setting it to 252,
but I'm not sure why that should be (256 works fine).

Anyways, regarding my problem of not being able to format the disks
with the RedHat Installation method, I solved it again by using an
external disk (i.e., installing RedHat on that disk, using the
utilities on the disk to do the formatting of the primary disk, and
then just skipping the format step in the RedHat installation).  

I really can't see how this is different from using a floppy with the
same kernel, fdisk, and mke2fs programs as the working system.

Thanks to Michal Jaegermann for his help.

