On Fri, 8 May 1998, Ian Kinner wrote:

> Perhaps we should set up an autoresponder for keyword "__builtin_memset" :)

I vote that someone explain which flavor of gcc supports this as a built
in.  I've tried

gcc-2.7.2
egcs-1.0.1
egcs-1.0.2

and the error occurs with all of them.  Someone else on the list commented
that they saw the problem with gcc-2.8.x.  That about ties it up.

> Your problem lies in arch/asm-alpha/string.h
> 
> Comment out the lines that test for gcc 2.8.1 and the lines executed when
> 2.8.1 is found. It should work fine after that.

Agreed, here it is:

 (might not patch cleanly, but the intent should be clear)

--- linux/include/asm-alpha/string.h.orig	Fri Apr 10 06:25:33 1998
+++ linux/include/asm-alpha/string.h	Thu Apr  9 19:28:23 1998
@@ -24,7 +24,8 @@
 extern void * __constant_c_memset(void *, unsigned long, long);
 extern void * __memset(void *, char, size_t);
 
-#if __GNUC__ > 2 || __GNUC_MINOR__ >= 8
+/* #if __GNUC__ > 2 || __GNUC_MINOR__ >= 8 */
+#if 0
 #define memset(s, c, n)							    \
 (__builtin_constant_p(c)						    \
  ? (__builtin_constant_p(n) && (c) == 0					    \


