> the keyboard on RedHat to emulate these key when I do a telnet to this
> machine?

'man loadkeys', 'man keycodes' and related.  Linux comes with some
50 different keyboard definitions and you can add some your own.
'man terminfo' and 'man termcap' will explain you how to define
terminals the other way around.  In short - you may define your
keyboard to send any sequences of bytes you want.

No, this has nothing to do with Red Hat, or even Alpha.

