>>> JOHN PRICE said:
>
> I successfully used the 5.0 disks on my multia to do a ftp install.  I
> did have to get the latest ramdisk.img from the updates directory.
> 
> On Tuesday, May 26, 1998 4:27 PM, Mark Conway wrote:
> > 
> > Note that you should use the *4.2* boot disk, as the 5.0 for the multia
> > was compiled accidentally with the Tulip ethernet driver.  This will
> > probably fix your problem....
> > 
> > On Tue, 26 May 1998, Peter Schmidt wrote:
> > 
> > > I'm trying to do a net install with my Multia on a 10base2 network.  The
> > > UDB ethernet is not sensing the network.

The problem of the RH 5.0 UDB kernel and some kinds of network connections
has been well known for quite some time.

The "tulip.c" driver was chosen for the 5.0 kernels because, at that time,
it was (considered to be) the only driver that would work on all the DEC
TULIP chip-based cards and builtins. We know that to be wrong, now... :-\

The accepted work-around is indeed to utilize the 4.2 UDB kernel, which has
the "de4x5.c" driver which will work with all the possible connection types
of the UDB hardware.

--Jay++

