DEXPORT_SYMTAB -c ftape_syms.c
In file included from /usr/src/linux/include/linux/sched.h:434,
                 from ../../include/linux/ftape.h:37,
                 from ftape_syms.c:32:
/usr/src/linux/include/asm/current.h:4: global register variable follows
a function definition
/usr/src/linux/include/asm/current.h:4: warning: call-clobbered register
used for global register variable

What really confuses me is that this error never shows up in compiling
the kernel and the kernel code also includes linux/sched.h which
includes asm/current.h, which has the following line:

register struct task_struct *current __asm__("$8");

Has anyone else encountered this error?

