> Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 494301622c230000
> Fsck.ext2(15) : Oops 0
> Pc = [<ffffc000033d080>] ps = 0000
> Rp = [<ffffc000033dc64>] sp = fffffc0003e319f8
> R0= 494301622c230000 r1=a43d8240f4351efe r2=fff r3=fff
> R8= 12015e000
> R16= 801 r17=ae0e7 r18=400 r19=2000
> R20=0 r21=11ffffc50 r22=0 r23=fffffc00003438f0
> R24=78 r25=2 r26=fffffc000033dc64 r27=fffffc000033dc08
> R28=0 r29=fffffc0000496e90 r30=fffffc0003e319f8
> Code : 47ff041f  47ff041f  47ff041f <a4200000> 402b0521 f4200019  40011402  4440d101  e4210000
> 
> And after that it usually freeze. I'd like to try to solve the proble, but I don't know where to begin .... On this example, fsck was the origine of the problem ... but it is not always this prog ....
> 


Try resetting your memory size a little smaller in milo before booting and
see if the paging errors go away:

milo> set MEMORY_SIZE xxx

Where xxx is your memory size in MB minus 2-4MB. I had this problem in RH4.2 but 
not in RH5.0 and used 252 for a 256MB system and it cured the problem. Since
it's also gone in RH5.0, if you're not already there, might try that. Using
a newer milo is also supposed to fix it.

Wes


